      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Let $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$",
      "worked_solution": "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the first row of the identity matrix and adding $-9$ times the second row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-9){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-9{R}_{2}$ to $A.$",
